{"id":"thomas-stevens","title":"Around the World on a Bicycle","who":"Thomas Stevens","when":"1884–1886","vehicle":"Columbia penny-farthing (high-wheeler)","kind":"bike","color":"#475569","summary":"The first person to cycle round the world, on a high-wheeled penny-farthing with no gears and solid tyres: across the American West, Europe, Turkey and Persia, then India, China and Japan. The bikepacking pioneer.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Thomas Stevens (cyclist)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Stevens_(cyclist)"}],"approximate":"Main places from his book; the roads between them are approximate.","km":25650,"bbox":[-122.4074,22.2818,139.6344,54.7871],"stops":[{"name":"San Francisco","place":"San Francisco","at":[37.7879,-122.4075],"date":"Apr 1884","text":"Off from San Francisco on a 50-inch Columbia high-wheeler, with a change of socks and a revolver.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/15-mile_Penny_Farthing_Race%2C_Harvard_University_Cycling_Association_in_1887.png/500px-15-mile_Penny_Farthing_Race%2C_Harvard_University_Cycling_Association_in_1887.png","page":"Penny-farthing","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:15-mile_Penny_Farthing_Race%2C_Harvard_University_Cycling_Association_in_1887.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"The Rockies","place":"Laramie, Wyoming","at":[41.3116,-105.5918],"text":"Across the Sierra and the deserts, often pushing the bike along railway tracks.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Historicdowntownlaramiewyoming3.jpg/500px-Historicdowntownlaramiewyoming3.jpg","page":"Laramie, Wyoming","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historicdowntownlaramiewyoming3.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Chicago","place":"Chicago","at":[41.8756,-87.6244],"text":"Over the plains to the Great Lakes.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg/500px-Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg","page":"Chicago","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg","credit":"File:Chicago River ferry.jpg: John Picken derivative work: Georgfotoart","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Boston","place":"Boston","at":[42.3588,-71.0578],"date":"Aug 1884","text":"The first crossing of America by bicycle. He then decided to keep going round the world.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/ISH_WC_Boston4.jpg/500px-ISH_WC_Boston4.jpg","page":"Boston","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISH_WC_Boston4.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Liverpool","place":"Liverpool","at":[53.3933,-2.9166],"text":"By steamer to England.","by":"boat","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Pier_Head%2C_Liverpool_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3059094.jpg/500px-Pier_Head%2C_Liverpool_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3059094.jpg","page":"Liverpool","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pier_Head%2C_Liverpool_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3059094.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Vienna","place":"Vienna, Austria","at":[48.2084,16.3725],"text":"Across England, France and Germany to the Danube.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg/500px-Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg","page":"Vienna","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg","credit":"Superbass","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Constantinople","place":"Istanbul, Turkey","at":[41.0064,28.9759],"text":"Through the Balkans to the Bosphorus.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg/500px-Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg","page":"Istanbul","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Anatolia","place":"Ankara, Turkey","at":[39.9208,32.854],"text":"Across Anatolia, where crowds gathered to see the strange machine.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Ankara_from_bus_station.jpg/500px-Ankara_from_bus_station.jpg","page":"Ankara","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ankara_from_bus_station.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Tehran","place":"Tehran, Iran","at":[35.6893,51.3896],"text":"Winter in Persia as a guest of the Shah's court. Refused passage through Afghanistan, he turned back.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/North_of_Tehran_Skyline_view.jpg/500px-North_of_Tehran_Skyline_view.jpg","page":"Tehran","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:North_of_Tehran_Skyline_view.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"India","place":"Kolkata, India","at":[22.5726,88.3639],"text":"By sea to India, then riding the Grand Trunk Road.","by":"boat","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Grand_Trunk_Road_Route.png/500px-Grand_Trunk_Road_Route.png","page":"Grand Trunk Road","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Trunk_Road_Route.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Hong Kong","place":"Hong Kong","at":[22.2818,114.1583],"text":"On to China by ship.","by":"boat"},{"name":"China","place":"Shanghai, China","at":[31.2313,121.47],"text":"A hard, sometimes hostile ride through southern China.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Huangpu_Park_20124-Shanghai_%2832208802494%29.jpg/500px-Huangpu_Park_20124-Shanghai_%2832208802494%29.jpg","page":"Shanghai","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huangpu_Park_20124-Shanghai_%2832208802494%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Comm